{"entryId":"3241","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3241:1","sourceSha256":"dbb7810ea1978fa39b0eab20deb1dba1bb2ccb75e310f131ff165a163f59c588","englishSha256":"4dbb4f61e696ea8292e52d0a505fd301e7735cb645b48a81a834077431363687","citations":[{"id":"3241:1:link-001","he":[0,559],"en":[1078,1091],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.6"},"reference":"Chullin 110a:6","assessment":"Hullin directly has the identity equivalence, arrival, boundary exchange and tefillin. The borrowed cloak, court intervention and concluding exchange continue onto 110b. Heilprin abbreviates the issues in the middle. Keep the historical speaker and each quotation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 110a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3241:1:link-002","he":[561,660],"en":[1093,1240],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_29b.2"},"reference":"Menachot 29b:2","assessment":"Menahot names Raami bar Tamrei as father-in-law, and describes the interrupted letter. The relation differs across the two passages.","evidence":[{"reference":"Menachot 29b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_29b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3241:1:link-003","he":[662,700],"en":[1241,1293],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_80a.8"},"reference":"Yevamot 80a:8","assessment":"The name and direction are explicit.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yevamot 80a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_80a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2],"holds":[{"raw":"דהוא חמוהי דרמי בר דיקולי","reason":"The Menahot relationship and the Hullin equivalence are both direct, and whether they concern the same people remains open.","evidence":[{"reference":"Menachot 29b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_29b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The narrative continues over 110a–b, and Menahot directly gives a relationship incompatible with Hullin’s equivalence if they refer to the same people. Preserve both.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 110a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 110a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"r